{"Annotation cleanup logs routine batch progress using r.log.Error() even when there is no error, and it logs full ids slices which can be extremely large. This will spam error logs and can massively increase log volume/memory usage when batch sizes are high.": 0.9863623976707458, "CleanUpService.Run now schedules the full cleanup suite every 1 minute instead of every 10 minutes, increasing DB/IO load across multiple cleanup jobs. Because each run has a 9-minute timeout, a slow run can effectively cause near-continuous cleanup execution.": 0.9134282469749451, "TestIntegrationAnnotationCleanUp registers t.Cleanup only after inserting and asserting records; if setup fails before reaching t.Cleanup (e.g., any require.NoError inside createTestAnnotations), the DB cleanup handler is never registered. This can leave rows behind and contaminate subsequent subtests that reuse the same test DB instance.": 0.9175292253494263, "The test case named for SQLite's SQLITE_MAX_VARIABLE_NUMBER runs unconditionally and uses db.InitTestDB, which may create MySQL/Postgres DBs based on GRAFANA_TEST_DB. On non-SQLite backends this still inserts 40k rows and sets a 32,767 batch size, making the test unnecessarily heavy and exercising a different deletion path than the one it claims to validate.": 0.7859340906143188}